TEXT -1016 48 Left 2 ;Votage profile with l_batt and c_batt (shunt reactor and capacitor bank)\n \nUpper circuit:\n \nInductive power flows from the two voltage sources\nto the l_batt element. Since the voltage is larger than \nthe nominal voltage (110kV) of the l_batt the sum of the two reactive\npowers is slightly more than 50MVAR (53MVAR)\nIf inductive power flows through a inductance the voltage\nat the other end decreases. So the voltage drops and the\nminimal value is reached at the l_batt element (shunt reactor)\nSince the line element is also inductive along the line the \nvoltage also drops slightly  \n \n \nLower circuit:\n \nCapacitive power flows from the two voltage sources\nto the c_batt element. Since the voltage is larger than\nthe nominal voltage (110kV) of the c_batt the sum of the two reacitve\npowers is more than -50MVAR (-56MVAR)\nIf capacitive power flows through a capacitance the voltage\nat the other end increases. So the voltage increase if their\nmaximal value is reached at the capacitor bank.\nSince the line element is also inductive along the line the\nvoltage also increase slightly
